  "AICL is the licensing and transaction layer built on top of AICR. Where AICR declares what is allowed, AICL defines how permission is actually obtained: license tiers and prices, quote and payment endpoints, signed license tokens, usage and audit logs, and revocation. It is designed to interoperate with emerging machine-payment mechanisms such as HTTP 402 flows and pay-per-crawl schemes, with agentic payment kept inside human-approved budgets and audit trails.": "AICL se kouch lisans ak tranzaksyon ki bati sou AICR. Kote AICR deklare sa ki pèmèt, AICL defini kijan yon otorizasyon reyèlman jwenn: nivo lisans ak pri, pwen final pou demann pri ak peman, token lisans siyen, jounal itilizasyon ak odit, ak revokasyon. Li fèt pou entewopere avèk nouvo mekanis peman machin tankou fli HTTP 402 ak sistèm pay-per-crawl, ak peman ajan ki toujou rete anndan bidjè yon moun apwouve ak tras odit.",
